abstract: >-
  EACH-based Cluster-Head (CH) selection relies on limited probabilistic rules. 
  This work models CH selection in an Improved-LEACH architecture as a three-objective problem 
  (energy, intra-cluster distance, packet loss) and adapts the lightweight Optimization by Morphological Filters 
  (OMF) metaheuristic for the first time. OMF-LEACH outperforms MOPSO and matches NSGA-II in network lifetime, 
  while reducing computation time by 11–28%. This demonstrates OMF's efficiency for multi-objective optimization 
  in resource-constrained wireless sensor networks.
